## UX Design Principles

### Button Hierarchy & Placement

**Primary, Secondary, and Tertiary Actions**

- **Primary Action**: One per screen, most prominent (filled button with primary color)
- **Secondary Actions**: Supporting actions (outlined buttons)
- **Tertiary Actions**: Less important (ghost/text buttons)

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Clear button hierarchy
<div className="flex gap-3 justify-end">
  <Button variant="ghost" onClick={onCancel}>
    Cancel
  </Button>
  <Button variant="outline" onClick={onSaveDraft}>
    Save Draft
  </Button>
  <Button onClick={onPublish}>
    Publish
  </Button>
</div>

// ❌ DON'T: All buttons look the same
<div className="flex gap-3">
  <Button>Cancel</Button>
  <Button>Save Draft</Button>
  <Button>Publish</Button>
</div>
```

**Button Placement Rules**

- Place primary actions on the **right** in dialogs/forms (natural reading flow)
- Destructive actions should be **separated** or require confirmation
- Group related actions together
- Use consistent placement across the app
- Mobile: Full-width buttons at bottom, primary action on top

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Proper destructive action handling
<AlertDialog>
  <AlertDialogContent>
    <AlertDialogHeader>
      <AlertDialogTitle>Delete Account</AlertDialogTitle>
      <AlertDialogDescription>
        This action cannot be undone. This will permanently delete your account.
      </AlertDialogDescription>
    </AlertDialogHeader>
    <AlertDialogFooter>
      <AlertDialogCancel>Cancel</AlertDialogCancel>
      <AlertDialogAction 
        className="bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground"
        onClick={onDelete}
      >
        Delete Account
      </AlertDialogAction>
    </AlertDialogFooter>
  </AlertDialogContent>
</AlertDialog>
```

### Call-to-Action (CTA) Best Practices

**CTA Copy Guidelines**

- Use **action verbs** (Create, Start, Get, Join, etc.)
- Be **specific** about what happens (not just "Submit" or "Click Here")
- Keep it **short** (1-3 words)
- Create **urgency** when appropriate (limited time/spots)
- Use **first person** for personal actions ("Create My Account" vs "Create Account")

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Clear, action-oriented CTAs
<Button>Start Free Trial</Button>
<Button>Create Project</Button>
<Button>Download Report</Button>
<Button>Invite Team Members</Button>

// ❌ DON'T: Vague or passive CTAs
<Button>Submit</Button>
<Button>Click Here</Button>
<Button>Continue</Button>
<Button>OK</Button>
```

**CTA Visibility**

- Primary CTAs should be **immediately visible** without scrolling (above the fold)
- Use **contrasting colors** that stand out from the background
- Ensure adequate **size** (min 44x44px touch target on mobile)
- Add appropriate **spacing** around CTAs (not cluttered)

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Prominent CTA with proper spacing
<div className="container max-w-4xl py-12">
  <div className="space-y-8">
    <div className="space-y-4 text-center">
      <h1 className="text-4xl font-bold">Ready to get started?</h1>
      <p className="text-lg text-muted-foreground">
        Join thousands of teams already using our platform
      </p>
    </div>
    
    <div className="flex justify-center">
      <Button size="lg" className="min-w-[200px]">
        Start Free Trial
      </Button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

### Form UX

**TanStack Form Standards**

- Use TanStack Form + Zod for all forms
- Follow shadcn TanStack Form patterns: https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/forms/tanstack-form
- Use `useForm` with `validators` and `form.Field` render props
- Prefer `onBlur` validation; keep `onSubmit` validation for final checks
- Always set `data-invalid` on `<Field />` and `aria-invalid` on controls
- Use `FieldGroup`, `FieldLabel`, `FieldDescription`, `FieldError` for structure
- Use `mode="array"` for arrays and `pushValue/removeValue` helpers

**Field Organization**

- Group related fields together with clear sections
- Show only **essential fields** initially (progressive disclosure)
- Use single-column layouts for forms (easier to scan)
- Place labels **above** fields (better for mobile)
- Show field requirements **upfront** (not after error)

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Well-organized form with clear sections
<form
  onSubmit={(e) => {
    e.preventDefault()
    form.handleSubmit()
  }}
  className="space-y-8"
>
  <div className="space-y-4">
    <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold">Personal Information</h3>

    <FieldGroup>
      <form.Field
        name="fullName"
        children={(field) => {
          const isInvalid =
            field.state.meta.isTouched && !field.state.meta.isValid
          return (
            <Field data-invalid={isInvalid}>
              <FieldLabel htmlFor={field.name}>Full Name</FieldLabel>
              <Input
                id={field.name}
                name={field.name}
                value={field.state.value}
                onBlur={field.handleBlur}
                onChange={(e) => field.handleChange(e.target.value)}
                aria-invalid={isInvalid}
                placeholder="John Doe"
              />
              {isInvalid && <FieldError errors={field.state.meta.errors} />}
            </Field>
          )
        }}
      />

      <form.Field
        name="email"
        children={(field) => {
          const isInvalid =
            field.state.meta.isTouched && !field.state.meta.isValid
          return (
            <Field data-invalid={isInvalid}>
              <FieldLabel htmlFor={field.name}>Email</FieldLabel>
              <Input
                id={field.name}
                name={field.name}
                type="email"
                value={field.state.value}
                onBlur={field.handleBlur}
                onChange={(e) => field.handleChange(e.target.value)}
                aria-invalid={isInvalid}
                placeholder="john@example.com"
              />
              <FieldDescription>
                We'll never share your email with anyone else.
              </FieldDescription>
              {isInvalid && <FieldError errors={field.state.meta.errors} />}
            </Field>
          )
        }}
      />
    </FieldGroup>
  </div>

  <Separator />

  <div className="space-y-4">
    <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold">Account Settings</h3>
    {/* More fields */}
  </div>

  <div className="flex justify-end gap-3">
    <Button type="button" variant="outline" onClick={onCancel}>
      Cancel
    </Button>
    <Button type="submit" disabled={form.state.isSubmitting}>
      {form.state.isSubmitting ? 'Creating Account...' : 'Create Account'}
    </Button>
  </div>
</form>
```

**Real-time Validation & Feedback**

- Validate **on blur** for most fields (not while typing)
- Show **success states** for valid fields when appropriate
- Provide **helpful error messages** (not just "Invalid")
- Show password strength indicators
- Display character counts for limited fields

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Helpful validation feedback
<form.Field
  name="username"
  children={(field) => {
    const isInvalid = field.state.meta.isTouched && !field.state.meta.isValid
    return (
      <Field data-invalid={isInvalid}>
        <FieldLabel htmlFor={field.name}>Username</FieldLabel>
        <div className="relative">
          <Input
            id={field.name}
            name={field.name}
            value={field.state.value}
            onBlur={field.handleBlur}
            onChange={(e) => field.handleChange(e.target.value)}
            aria-invalid={isInvalid}
          />
          {field.state.value && !isInvalid && (
            <CheckCircle className="absolute right-3 top-3 h-4 w-4 text-green-500" />
          )}
        </div>
        <FieldDescription>
          3-20 characters, letters and numbers only
        </FieldDescription>
        {isInvalid && <FieldError errors={field.state.meta.errors} />}
      </Field>
    )
  }}
/>
```

### Feedback & States

**User Feedback Patterns**

- Always provide **immediate feedback** for user actions
- Use **toast notifications** for success/error messages
- Show **loading states** during async operations
- Display **progress indicators** for multi-step processes
- Provide **empty states** with helpful guidance

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Comprehensive feedback handling
import { toast } from 'sonner';

const handleSave = async () => {
  try {
    setIsLoading(true);
    await saveDraft();
    toast.success('Draft saved successfully');
  } catch (error) {
    toast.error('Failed to save draft. Please try again.');
  } finally {
    setIsLoading(false);
  }
};

// Empty state example
{items.length === 0 ? (
  <div className="flex flex-col items-center justify-center py-12 text-center">
    <FileQuestion className="h-12 w-12 text-muted-foreground mb-4" />
    <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">No projects yet</h3>
    <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-6">
      Get started by creating your first project
    </p>
    <Button onClick={onCreateProject}>
      <Plus className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" />
      Create Project
    </Button>
  </div>
) : (
  <ProjectList items={items} />
)}
```

**Loading States**

- Use **skeleton screens** to maintain layout (prevents content jump)
- Show **progress percentages** for long operations
- Keep users informed with **status messages**
- Allow **cancellation** of long-running operations when possible
- Never block the entire UI unless absolutely necessary

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Non-blocking loading with context
<Card>
  <CardHeader>
    <CardTitle>Recent Activity</CardTitle>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent>
    {isLoading ? (
      <div className="space-y-4">
        {[...Array(3)].map((_, i) => (
          <div key={i} className="flex items-center space-x-4">
            <Skeleton className="h-12 w-12 rounded-full" />
            <div className="space-y-2 flex-1">
              <Skeleton className="h-4 w-full" />
              <Skeleton className="h-4 w-2/3" />
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    ) : (
      <ActivityList items={activities} />
    )}
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

### Navigation & Information Architecture

**Navigation Patterns**

- Keep navigation **consistent** across all pages
- Highlight **current location** (active states)
- Use **breadcrumbs** for deep hierarchies
- Provide **clear exit points** from flows
- Make important actions **easily accessible** (max 2 clicks)

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Clear navigation with active states
<nav className="flex items-center space-x-1">
  <NavigationMenu>
    <NavigationMenuList>
      <NavigationMenuItem>
        <Link href="/dashboard" className={cn(
          "px-4 py-2 rounded-md text-sm font-medium transition-colors",
          pathname === "/dashboard" 
            ? "bg-accent text-accent-foreground" 
            : "text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground"
        )}>
          Dashboard
        </Link>
      </NavigationMenuItem>
      <NavigationMenuItem>
        <Link href="/projects" className={cn(
          "px-4 py-2 rounded-md text-sm font-medium transition-colors",
          pathname.startsWith("/projects")
            ? "bg-accent text-accent-foreground"
            : "text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground"
        )}>
          Projects
        </Link>
      </NavigationMenuItem>
    </NavigationMenuList>
  </NavigationMenu>
</nav>

// Breadcrumbs for deep navigation
<Breadcrumb>
  <BreadcrumbList>
    <BreadcrumbItem>
      <BreadcrumbLink href="/dashboard">Dashboard</BreadcrumbLink>
    </BreadcrumbItem>
    <BreadcrumbSeparator />
    <BreadcrumbItem>
