```

### Content Hierarchy & Typography

**Visual Hierarchy**

- Use size, weight, and color to establish **importance**
- Maintain consistent **heading levels** (h1 → h2 → h3)
- Keep **line length** readable (45-75 characters)
- Use adequate **line height** (1.5-1.7 for body text)
- Implement proper **spacing** between sections

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Clear visual hierarchy
<div className="space-y-8">
  <div className="space-y-2">
    <h1 className="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Page Title</h1>
    <p className="text-lg text-muted-foreground">
      Brief description or subtitle providing context
    </p>
  </div>

  <Separator />

  <div className="space-y-6">
    <div className="space-y-4">
      <h2 className="text-2xl font-semibold">Section Heading</h2>
      <p className="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        Body content with proper line height and spacing for optimal readability.
        This text should be easy to scan and digest.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div className="space-y-4">
      <h3 className="text-xl font-semibold">Subsection</h3>
      <p className="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
        More detailed content...
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

### Interactive Elements

**Hover & Focus States**

- Always provide **clear hover states** for interactive elements
- Ensure **focus indicators** are visible for keyboard navigation
- Use **cursor changes** to indicate interactivity (`cursor-pointer`)
- Add **smooth transitions** for state changes
- Maintain **adequate touch targets** (min 44x44px on mobile)

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Clear interactive states
<Card 
  className="transition-all hover:shadow-lg hover:border-primary cursor-pointer focus-within:ring-2 focus-within:ring-primary"
  onClick={onClick}
  tabIndex={0}
  onKeyDown={(e) => e.key === 'Enter' && onClick()}
>
  <CardContent className="p-6">
    <h3 className="font-semibold group-hover:text-primary transition-colors">
      Interactive Card
    </h3>
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

**Disabled States**

- Clearly indicate **disabled state** with reduced opacity
- Provide **tooltip explanation** for why something is disabled
- Consider using **helpful error messages** instead of just disabling
- Never disable without communicating why

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Disabled state with explanation
<TooltipProvider>
  <Tooltip>
    <TooltipTrigger asChild>
      <div>
        <Button disabled={!hasPermission} className="w-full">
          Delete Project
        </Button>
      </div>
    </TooltipTrigger>
    {!hasPermission && (
      <TooltipContent>
        <p>You don't have permission to delete this project</p>
      </TooltipContent>
    )}
  </Tooltip>
</TooltipProvider>
```

### Error Handling & Recovery

**Error Messages**

- Write **human-friendly** error messages (avoid technical jargon)
- Explain **what went wrong** and **how to fix it**
- Provide **actionable next steps**
- Use appropriate **error severity** (info, warning, error)
- Show errors **inline** near the relevant field/section

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Helpful error messages
{error && (
  <Alert variant="destructive">
    <AlertCircle className="h-4 w-4" />
    <AlertTitle>Unable to save changes</AlertTitle>
    <AlertDescription className="space-y-2">
      <p>Your session has expired. Please sign in again to continue.</p>
      <Button 
        variant="outline" 
        size="sm" 
        onClick={() => router.push('/sign-in')}
      >
        Sign In
      </Button>
    </AlertDescription>
  </Alert>
)}

// ❌ DON'T: Cryptic error messages
{error && (
  <div className="text-red-500">
    Error 401: Unauthorized
  </div>
)}
```

**Recovery Options**

- Always provide a **way forward** after an error
- Offer **retry** functionality for failed operations
- Preserve **user input** when errors occur
- Provide **help links** or support contact when appropriate

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Error with recovery options
{error && (
  <div className="flex flex-col items-center justify-center py-12 space-y-4">
    <AlertCircle className="h-12 w-12 text-destructive" />
    <div className="text-center space-y-2">
      <h3 className="font-semibold">Failed to load projects</h3>
      <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        We couldn't load your projects. This might be a temporary issue.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div className="flex gap-3">
      <Button variant="outline" onClick={onRetry}>
        Try Again
      </Button>
      <Button variant="ghost" onClick={onContactSupport}>
        Contact Support
      </Button>
    </div>
  </div>
)}
```

### Mobile-First & Responsive Design

**Mobile Considerations**

- Design for **mobile first**, then enhance for desktop
- Use **full-width buttons** on mobile when appropriate
- Ensure **adequate spacing** for touch targets (44x44px minimum)
- Make **navigation accessible** with hamburger menu when needed
- Stack elements **vertically** on mobile, horizontal on desktop

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Responsive layout with mobile-first approach
<div className="space-y-6">
  <div className="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
    <div className="space-y-1">
      <h2 className="text-2xl font-semibold">Projects</h2>
      <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Manage your projects and settings
      </p>
    </div>
    <Button className="w-full sm:w-auto">
      <Plus className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" />
      New Project
    </Button>
  </div>

  <div className="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    {projects.map((project) => (
      <ProjectCard key={project.id} project={project} />
    ))}
  </div>
</div>
```

### Accessibility (A11y)

**ARIA & Semantic HTML**

- Use **semantic HTML** elements (button, nav, main, article)
- Add **ARIA labels** for screen readers when needed
- Ensure **keyboard navigation** works everywhere
- Provide **alt text** for all images
- Maintain proper **heading hierarchy**

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Accessible interactive elements
<button
  onClick={onClose}
  aria-label="Close dialog"
  className="absolute right-4 top-4 rounded-sm opacity-70 transition-opacity hover:opacity-100"
>
  <X className="h-4 w-4" />
  <span className="sr-only">Close</span>
</button>

// Accessible form with proper labels
<form.Field
  name="email"
  children={(field) => {
    const isInvalid = field.state.meta.isTouched && !field.state.meta.isValid
    return (
      <Field data-invalid={isInvalid}>
        <FieldLabel htmlFor={field.name}>Email Address</FieldLabel>
        <Input
          id={field.name}
          name={field.name}
          type="email"
          autoComplete="email"
          value={field.state.value}
          onBlur={field.handleBlur}
          onChange={(e) => field.handleChange(e.target.value)}
          aria-describedby={`${field.name}-description ${field.name}-error`}
          aria-invalid={isInvalid}
        />
        <FieldDescription id={`${field.name}-description`}>
          We'll use this to contact you
        </FieldDescription>
        {isInvalid && (
          <FieldError id={`${field.name}-error`} errors={field.state.meta.errors} />
        )}
      </Field>
    )
  }}
/>
```

### Confirmation & Destructive Actions

**Confirmation Dialogs**

- Always **confirm destructive actions** (delete, remove, etc.)
- Clearly state **what will be affected**
- Explain **consequences** (e.g., "This cannot be undone")
- Make users **type to confirm** for critical actions
- Use **appropriate button colors** (destructive red for delete)

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Proper confirmation for destructive action
<AlertDialog>
  <AlertDialogTrigger asChild>
    <Button variant="destructive" size="sm">
      <Trash2 className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" />
      Delete Project
    </Button>
  </AlertDialogTrigger>
  <AlertDialogContent>
    <AlertDialogHeader>
      <AlertDialogTitle>Are you absolutely sure?</AlertDialogTitle>
      <AlertDialogDescription className="space-y-2">
        <p>
          This will permanently delete the <strong>{projectName}</strong> project
          and all of its data.
        </p>
        <p className="text-destructive font-medium">
          This action cannot be undone.
        </p>
      </AlertDialogDescription>
    </AlertDialogHeader>
    <AlertDialogFooter>
      <AlertDialogCancel>Cancel</AlertDialogCancel>
      <AlertDialogAction
        className="bg-destructive text-destructive-foreground hover:bg-destructive/90"
        onClick={onDelete}
      >
        Delete Project
      </AlertDialogAction>
    </AlertDialogFooter>
  </AlertDialogContent>
</AlertDialog>
```

### Progressive Disclosure

**Show Information Gradually**

- Don't **overwhelm users** with all options at once
- Use **accordions** for optional/advanced settings
- Implement **multi-step forms** for complex processes
- Show **tooltips** for additional context
- Use **"Show more"** patterns for long lists

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Progressive disclosure with accordion
<Accordion type="single" collapsible>
  <AccordionItem value="basic">
    <AccordionTrigger>Basic Settings</AccordionTrigger>
    <AccordionContent>
      {/* Essential settings */}
    </AccordionContent>
  </AccordionItem>
  
  <AccordionItem value="advanced">
    <AccordionTrigger>
      <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
        Advanced Settings
        <Badge variant="outline" className="text-xs">Optional</Badge>
      </div>
    </AccordionTrigger>
    <AccordionContent>
      {/* Advanced options */}
    </AccordionContent>
  </AccordionItem>
</Accordion>
```

### Micro-interactions & Animations

**Purposeful Animations**

- Use animations to **guide attention** and provide feedback
- Keep animations **subtle and fast** (150-300ms)
- Animate **meaningful transitions** (page changes, state updates)
- Provide **reduced motion** option for accessibility
- Never animate just for decoration

```tsx
// ✅ DO: Purposeful micro-interactions
<Button
  className={cn(
    "transition-all duration-200",
    "hover:scale-105 active:scale-95",
    "hover:shadow-md"
  )}
  onClick={onSave}
>
  Save Changes
</Button>

// Animate list items
<motion.div
  initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 20 }}
  animate={{ opacity: 1, y: 0 }}
  exit={{ opacity: 0, y: -20 }}
  transition={{ duration: 0.2 }}
>
  <Card>{/* content */}</Card>
</motion.div>
```

## Best Practices

1. **Use shadcn/ui components** wherever applicable
2. **Follow the existing component structure** in the project
3. **Use semantic HTML** and ARIA attributes for accessibility
4. **Optimize images** with Next.js Image component
5. **Use server components** by default, client components when needed
6. **Implement error boundaries** for error handling
7. **Follow ESLint rules** and Prettier formatting
8. **Write self-documenting code** with clear naming
9. **Keep components small** (< 200 lines ideally)
10. **Extract complex logic** into hooks or utility functions
11. **Design mobile-first** and enhance progressively for larger screens
12. **Always provide user feedback** for actions and state changes
13. **Use clear visual hierarchy** with proper typography and spacing
14. **Make interactive elements obviously clickable** with proper states
15. **Confirm destructive actions** and provide recovery options